forgejo (17.0.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  The "main" component follows every Forgejo release, including the new
  major version that comes about every three months. On its first start, a
  new major migrates the database, and that can't be undone: the previous
  version doesn't run on the migrated database, so going back means
  restoring a backup. Take one before upgrading to a new major:

    cd /var/lib/forgejo && sudo -u git forgejo dump

  (it writes forgejo-dump-<time>.zip there). For fewer of these upgrades,
  use the "lts" component instead: it stays on Forgejo's long-term support
  release, with its patch releases only, and moves on to the next one about
  once a year, which is a major upgrade like the others.

 -- freshdeb <packages@freshdeb.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
